   "kind": "plaque",
   "plaque": "aintree_grand_national",
   "title": "The Grand National",
   "text": "THE GRAND NATIONAL. Run at Aintree since 1839, over about four and a quarter miles and thirty fences. Becher's Brook is named after Captain Martin Becher, who fell there in that first race and is said to have hidden in the brook while the rest of the field jumped over him."
  },
  {
   "x": 15,
   "y": 8,
   "plaque": "aintree_red_rum",
   "title": "Red Rum",
   "text": "RED RUM. Won the Grand National in 1973, 1974 and 1977, and came second in the two years between. Trained by Ginger McCain, who galloped him on the sands at Southport. He is buried by the winning post here, facing the finish."
  }
 ],
